 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:33:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: report the coded format flags in ENUM_FMT
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The decoder's format table sets V4L2_FMT_FLAG_DYN_RESOLUTION and
V4L2_FMT_FLAG_CONTINUOUS_BYTESTREAM on the coded formats, but
vidioc_enum_fmt() only copies the fourcc, so applications never see
them.

GStreamer's v4l2 decoders read DYN_RESOLUTION to know that the driver
sends V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE once the header is parsed. Without it,
v4l2h264dec sets up the CAPTURE queue on its own, then takes that first
event for a resolution change in the middle of the stream. It stays
marked as draining, and the next flush (a seek) throws the CAPTURE pool
away and asks for a new one. Copy the flags.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index cfc1694e7..e151b5a39 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -327,6 +327,7 @@ static int vidioc_enum_fmt(struct file *file, struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f,
 	if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(formats))
 		return -EINVAL;
 	f->pixelformat = formats[i].fourcc;
+	f->flags = formats[i].flags;
 	return 0;
 }
 
